{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memory is wired into your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call. Now you want to see whether it actually recalls\nanything, get that activity into your own logs, and know that a slow or broken store\nwon't take down the chat. This page covers the middleware's options and how to observe\nand operate it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New to memory? Start with the "},{"type":"link","href":"./overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"./quickstart","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quickstart"}]},{"type":"text","value":" first."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"memorymiddleware-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MemoryAdapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(required)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The backend to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":" from and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":" to."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scope"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MemoryScope | (ctx) => MemoryScope"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(required)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Isolation scope, static or derived per request."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"role"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'recall+save' | 'save-only'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'recall+save'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'save-only'"},{"type":"text","value":" persists turns without recalling or injecting."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRecall"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"({ scope, query, result }) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"App telemetry after each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSave"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"({ scope, turn, receipts }) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"App telemetry after each deferred "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every option in one place:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\n\nconst mw = memoryMiddleware({\n  adapter: inMemory(),\n  // Function form derives scope per request. `ctx.threadId` is the stable\n  // per-conversation id; add `userId` from your server-validated session.\n  scope: (ctx) => ({ threadId: ctx.threadId }),\n  role: 'recall+save', // or 'save-only' to persist without injecting\n  onRecall: ({ query, result }) => {\n    console.log('recalled', result.fragments?.length ?? 0, 'hits for', query)\n  },\n  onSave: ({ receipts }) => {\n    console.log('saved', receipts.filter((r) => r.ok).length, 'records')\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"persist-without-recalling","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persist without recalling"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default the middleware both recalls and saves ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"role: 'recall+save'"},{"type":"text","value":"). Set\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"role: 'save-only'"},{"type":"text","value":" to persist each turn without reading memory back or injecting anything\ninto the prompt. Use it to build up a user's history before you turn recall on, or on\nroutes where you want to record turns but not shape the current answer."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"telemetry-with-onrecall-and-onsave","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Telemetry with onRecall and onSave"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The devtools events below are for watching memory during development. For telemetry that\nships with your app, use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRecall"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSave"},{"type":"text","value":" callbacks shown above. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRecall"},{"type":"text","value":"\nfires after each recall with the query and result, so you can count hits. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSave"},{"type":"text","value":" fires\nafter each deferred save with the write receipts, so you can count writes. Send those to\nyour metrics client instead of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"console.log"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"watch-it-in-devtools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Watch it in devtools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The AI DevTools has a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memory"}]},{"type":"text","value":" tab for any chat wired with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":". It\nshows each turn's recall (query, fragment count, characters injected, recall duration)\nand, for adapters that implement "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inspect"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listFacts"},{"type":"text","value":" (the built-in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inMemory()"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redis()"},{"type":"text","value":" do), the current stored records and facts. See the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../getting-started/devtools#memory-inspector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memory Inspector"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for what it renders and\nhow server-side memory reaches the panel."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Under the hood the middleware emits these events on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aiEventClient"},{"type":"text","value":" (from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-event-client"},{"type":"text","value":"). The panel reads them, and you can subscribe directly:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Event"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memory:retrieve:started"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recall begins"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memory:retrieve:completed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recall returns (fragment count, whether tools were injected)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memory:persist:started"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A deferred save begins"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memory:persist:completed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A save completes (receipt count)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memory:error"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":" threw ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"phase: 'recall'"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'save'"},{"type":"text","value":"). Carries "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scope"},{"type":"text","value":" only when it was already resolved; omitted if the resolver failed or never ran."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"failures-are-non-fatal","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Failures are non-fatal"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A memory failure never breaks a chat run. A throwing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":" emits\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memory:error"},{"type":"text","value":" and the run continues with degraded memory: recall returns nothing, and a\nfailed save is dropped. Streaming is never blocked, and a failed save never fails the\nturn. This means a flaky store degrades the experience instead of taking down the chat."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"where-to-go-next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where to go next"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":" contract and how a turn flows"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapters"}]},{"type":"text","value":": every adapter's options, with an example of each"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./custom-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":": implement "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":" for a backend that isn't shipped"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"memorymiddleware-options","text":"memoryMiddleware options","level":2},{"id":"persist-without-recalling","text":"Persist without recalling","level":2},{"id":"telemetry-with-onrecall-and-onsave","text":"Telemetry with onRecall and onSave","level":2},{"id":"watch-it-in-devtools","text":"Watch it in devtools","level":2},{"id":"failures-are-non-fatal","text":"Failures are non-fatal","level":2},{"id":"where-to-go-next","text":"Where to go next","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nMemory is wired into your `chat()` call. Now you want to see whether it actually recalls\nanything, get that activity into your own logs, and know that a slow or broken store\nwon't take down the chat. This page covers the middleware's options and how to observe\nand operate it.\n\nNew to memory? Start with the [Overview](./overview) and [Quickstart](./quickstart) first.\n\n## `memoryMiddleware` options\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Purpose |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|\n| `adapter` | `MemoryAdapter` | (required) | The backend to `recall` from and `save` to. |\n| `scope` | `MemoryScope \\| (ctx) => MemoryScope` | (required) | Isolation scope, static or derived per request. |\n| `role` | `'recall+save' \\| 'save-only'` | `'recall+save'` | `'save-only'` persists turns without recalling or injecting. |\n| `onRecall` | `({ scope, query, result }) => void` | none | App telemetry after each `recall`. |\n| `onSave` | `({ scope, turn, receipts }) => void` | none | App telemetry after each deferred `save`. |\n\nEvery option in one place:\n\n```ts\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\n\nconst mw = memoryMiddleware({\n  adapter: inMemory(),\n  // Function form derives scope per request. `ctx.threadId` is the stable\n  // per-conversation id; add `userId` from your server-validated session.\n  scope: (ctx) => ({ threadId: ctx.threadId }),\n  role: 'recall+save', // or 'save-only' to persist without injecting\n  onRecall: ({ query, result }) => {\n    console.log('recalled', result.fragments?.length ?? 0, 'hits for', query)\n  },\n  onSave: ({ receipts }) => {\n    console.log('saved', receipts.filter((r) => r.ok).length, 'records')\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Persist without recalling\n\nBy default the middleware both recalls and saves (`role: 'recall+save'`). Set\n`role: 'save-only'` to persist each turn without reading memory back or injecting anything\ninto the prompt. Use it to build up a user's history before you turn recall on, or on\nroutes where you want to record turns but not shape the current answer.\n\n## Telemetry with onRecall and onSave\n\nThe devtools events below are for watching memory during development. For telemetry that\nships with your app, use the `onRecall` and `onSave` callbacks shown above. `onRecall`\nfires after each recall with the query and result, so you can count hits. `onSave` fires\nafter each deferred save with the write receipts, so you can count writes. Send those to\nyour metrics client instead of `console.log`.\n\n## Watch it in devtools\n\nThe AI DevTools has a **Memory** tab for any chat wired with `memoryMiddleware`. It\nshows each turn's recall (query, fragment count, characters injected, recall duration)\nand, for adapters that implement `inspect`/`listFacts` (the built-in `inMemory()` and\n`redis()` do), the current stored records and facts. See the\n[Memory Inspector](../getting-started/devtools#memory-inspector) for what it renders and\nhow server-side memory reaches the panel.\n\nUnder the hood the middleware emits these events on `aiEventClient` (from\n`@tanstack/ai-event-client`). The panel reads them, and you can subscribe directly:\n\n| Event | When |\n|-------|------|\n| `memory:retrieve:started` | Recall begins |\n| `memory:retrieve:completed` | Recall returns (fragment count, whether tools were injected) |\n| `memory:persist:started` | A deferred save begins |\n| `memory:persist:completed` | A save completes (receipt count) |\n| `memory:error` | A `recall` or `save` threw (`phase: 'recall'` or `'save'`). Carries `scope` only when it was already resolved; omitted if the resolver failed or never ran. |\n\n## Failures are non-fatal\n\nA memory failure never breaks a chat run. A throwing `recall` or `save` emits\n`memory:error` and the run continues with degraded memory: recall returns nothing, and a\nfailed save is dropped. Streaming is never blocked, and a failed save never fails the\nturn. This means a flaky store degrades the experience instead of taking down the chat.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Overview](./overview): the `recall`/`save` contract and how a turn flows\n- [Adapters](./adapters): every adapter's options, with an example of each\n- [Custom Adapter](./custom-adapter): implement `recall`/`save` for a backend that isn't shipped\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Operating\nid: memory-operating\norder: 5\ndescription: \"Run memoryMiddleware in production: configure its options, add onRecall/onSave telemetry, watch recall and save in devtools, and rely on non-fatal failure handling that never breaks a chat run.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - memory\n  - middleware options\n  - telemetry\n  - devtools\n  - observability\n  - save-only\n---\n\nMemory is wired into your `chat()` call. Now you want to see whether it actually recalls\nanything, get that activity into your own logs, and know that a slow or broken store\nwon't take down the chat. This page covers the middleware's options and how to observe\nand operate it.\n\nNew to memory? Start with the [Overview](./overview) and [Quickstart](./quickstart) first.\n\n## `memoryMiddleware` options\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Purpose |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|\n| `adapter` | `MemoryAdapter` | (required) | The backend to `recall` from and `save` to. |\n| `scope` | `MemoryScope \\| (ctx) => MemoryScope` | (required) | Isolation scope, static or derived per request. |\n| `role` | `'recall+save' \\| 'save-only'` | `'recall+save'` | `'save-only'` persists turns without recalling or injecting. |\n| `onRecall` | `({ scope, query, result }) => void` | none | App telemetry after each `recall`. |\n| `onSave` | `({ scope, turn, receipts }) => void` | none | App telemetry after each deferred `save`. |\n\nEvery option in one place:\n\n```ts\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\n\nconst mw = memoryMiddleware({\n  adapter: inMemory(),\n  // Function form derives scope per request. `ctx.threadId` is the stable\n  // per-conversation id; add `userId` from your server-validated session.\n  scope: (ctx) => ({ threadId: ctx.threadId }),\n  role: 'recall+save', // or 'save-only' to persist without injecting\n  onRecall: ({ query, result }) => {\n    console.log('recalled', result.fragments?.length ?? 0, 'hits for', query)\n  },\n  onSave: ({ receipts }) => {\n    console.log('saved', receipts.filter((r) => r.ok).length, 'records')\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Persist without recalling\n\nBy default the middleware both recalls and saves (`role: 'recall+save'`). Set\n`role: 'save-only'` to persist each turn without reading memory back or injecting anything\ninto the prompt. Use it to build up a user's history before you turn recall on, or on\nroutes where you want to record turns but not shape the current answer.\n\n## Telemetry with onRecall and onSave\n\nThe devtools events below are for watching memory during development. For telemetry that\nships with your app, use the `onRecall` and `onSave` callbacks shown above. `onRecall`\nfires after each recall with the query and result, so you can count hits. `onSave` fires\nafter each deferred save with the write receipts, so you can count writes. Send those to\nyour metrics client instead of `console.log`.\n\n## Watch it in devtools\n\nThe AI DevTools has a **Memory** tab for any chat wired with `memoryMiddleware`. It\nshows each turn's recall (query, fragment count, characters injected, recall duration)\nand, for adapters that implement `inspect`/`listFacts` (the built-in `inMemory()` and\n`redis()` do), the current stored records and facts. See the\n[Memory Inspector](../getting-started/devtools#memory-inspector) for what it renders and\nhow server-side memory reaches the panel.\n\nUnder the hood the middleware emits these events on `aiEventClient` (from\n`@tanstack/ai-event-client`). The panel reads them, and you can subscribe directly:\n\n| Event | When |\n|-------|------|\n| `memory:retrieve:started` | Recall begins |\n| `memory:retrieve:completed` | Recall returns (fragment count, whether tools were injected) |\n| `memory:persist:started` | A deferred save begins |\n| `memory:persist:completed` | A save completes (receipt count) |\n| `memory:error` | A `recall` or `save` threw (`phase: 'recall'` or `'save'`). Carries `scope` only when it was already resolved; omitted if the resolver failed or never ran. |\n\n## Failures are non-fatal\n\nA memory failure never breaks a chat run. A throwing `recall` or `save` emits\n`memory:error` and the run continues with degraded memory: recall returns nothing, and a\nfailed save is dropped. Streaming is never blocked, and a failed save never fails the\nturn. This means a flaky store degrades the experience instead of taking down the chat.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Overview](./overview): the `recall`/`save` contract and how a turn flows\n- [Adapters](./adapters): every adapter's options, with an example of each\n- [Custom Adapter](./custom-adapter): implement `recall`/`save` for a backend that isn't shipped\n"}
